  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure will build across the region this weekend with\nnice fall weather. Tonight's temperatures will be the coldest\ndropping down to the lower 30s for most locations south of the\nlakeshore. Freeze headlines remain in effect tonight for all \nlocations south of the immediate lakeshore. Sunny and cool\nweather is expected on Sunday with high temps around 60 degrees.\nMore areas of frost will be likely Sunday night into early \nMonday morning with temps in the lower to middle 30s. The \nweather pattern for the week ahead will be quiet and dry, with \nseasonably mild temperatures. High pressure will remain in \ncontrol over the Ohio Valley and Great Lakes region next week. \nHigh temperatures will be generally in the 60s to near 70 \ndegrees. Overnight low temps will be in the 30s to middle 40s.",
